      "message": "It seems odd to manually check `UNBUNDLED_BUILD_TARGET_SDK_WITH_API_FINGERPRINT` here inside the `java.UseApiFingerprint` conditional, when the output of `java.UseApiFingerprint` already depends on that environment variable.  There\u0027s also a lot of duplication of this code.  Maybe it would make sense to abstract all of this into a helper function that returns the correct value for `minSdkVersion`/`targetSdkVersion`, plus any required deps?  It would either need to take the default value of `minSdkVersion`/`targetSdkVersion` as a string, or return a bool if it wants to override the version:\n```\n    if fingerprintMinSdkVersion, fingerprintDeps, useFingerprint :\u003d java.ApiFingerprint(ctx); useFingerprint {\n        minSdkVersion \u003d fingerprintMinSdkVerion\n        implicitInputs \u003d append(implicitInputs, fingerprintDeps)\n    }\n```",
